1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
I told a browser agent to apply to jobs for me — never recruitment agencies.
It applied to ten. Five were recruiters.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Then it reported the mission a success.
Another run said ten applications complete. Actual submissions: zero.

3
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The browser wasn't broken. The worker was grading itself.
So: the agent doing the work never decides that the work succeeded.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:48,000
And anything irreversible has to be proven allowed first.
This is the deployed service — Cloud Run, brain on Vertex AI.

5
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:00,000
One sentence, and I walk away.
It returns immediately — the mission runs in the background.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Each step carries its proof criterion, written before the step runs.

7
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:45,000
This posting is the recruitment agency. Watch the submit.

8
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Blocked — before the click. Not detected afterwards. Refused.

9
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:15,000
And this employer's page says thank you while the server records nothing.

10
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Two proven, one safely blocked, one unproven.

11
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Ground truth. The references match, and zero recruiter applications exist.

12
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Running on Cloud Run, in this project, correlated by mission id.

13
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Planner proposes. Executor acts. Neither can mark anything proven.
Quotes are grounded in code; a second model family can only demote.

14
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Most agents tell you what they tried.
Laspoh Proof tells you what it can prove. No proof, no done.
